# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vivado per-project scratch directories — fully reproducible from the .xpr
# and the sources_1/ fileset.  Wildcarded so they apply to every kernel
# project under kernels/<name>_test/ without per-kernel maintenance.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.cache/
*.gen/
*.hw/
*.ip_user_files/
*.runs/
*.sim/

# Synthesis-checkpoint scratch under sources/ (large binary; regenerated).
# The middle slash anchors gitignore patterns, so `**/` is required to make
# this match the per-kernel kernels/<name>_test/<name>_test.srcs/utils_1/.
**/*.srcs/utils_1/

# Vivado bundled IP HDL.  Vivado dumps the .v / .sv / .vh / .vhd of every
# IP the block design references into <proj>.srcs/sources_1/bd/<bd>/ipshared/
# the first time the project is opened against an IP catalogue.  These files
# are regenerated on every checkout-and-open and can balloon into hundreds of
# files (e.g. a full second copy of MatmulKernel HDL when MatmulKernel sits
# upstream of the kernel's CTRL port).  Derived, never source.
**/*.srcs/sources_1/bd/*/ipshared/

# Vivado-generated project-regeneration script.  Vivado writes
# kernels/<k>_test/<k>_test.tcl the first time the project is opened (or via
# write_project_tcl) so the project can be rebuilt without the .xpr.  We
# treat the .xpr as the source of truth here, so the .tcl is scratch.  If a
# kernel ever needs a hand-authored .tcl in its project root, force-add it
# with `git add -f`.
kernels/*/*.tcl

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vivado / xsim session and log files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.jou
*.log
*.str
*.pb
*.wdb
*.backup.jou
*.backup.log
.Xil/
xsim.dir/
webtalk*.xml
webtalk*.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vivado waveform view configs (saved automatically when xsim exits;
# rarely worth tracking — force-add explicitly with `git add -f` if needed).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.wcfg
*.wcfg.bak

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test-stand outputs
#
# Default scoreboard report path is now <project_dir>/<kernel>_test_report.json
# (see scripts/run_tb.sh).  Reports are run artefacts, not source.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*_test_report.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS / misc
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
